          "selector": "OP=0x02 GG=0x03 II=zone RR=0x0013",
          "source": "decision_catalog",
          "reading": "SD-06 reads values 1 to 0x20 as a one-based circuit number and subtracts one; the formula holds for the laboratory scope only.",
          "scope": "LAB"
        },
        {
          "selector": "OP=0x02 GG=0x03 II=zone RR=0x001C",
          "source": "register_map",
          "reading": "The register map names this register zone_circuit_assignment: a raw one-byte index kept without renumbering, with a signed reading in which -1 means not bound as a candidate.",
          "scope": "PROFILE"
        }
      ],
      "reason": "The zone's circuit-assignment register RR=0x001C is the basis of the supply relation from the thermal circuit to the zone. RR=0x0013 is also the room-unit binding of SD-05 and is no basis here.",
      "pending_review": null,
